---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Giovanni Vega Garcia',
  alternateName: 'Gio',
  jobTitle: 'Founder',
  worksFor: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Vemor', url: 'https://vemor.ai' },
  knowsLanguage: ['en', 'es'],
  alumniOf: [
    { '@type': 'CollegeOrUniversity', name: 'University of San Diego' },
  ],
  description: '14-year automotive operations veteran turned AI automation builder. MBA (University of San Diego), GenAI certificate (IE Business School). Founder of Vemor Consulting LLC, San Diego.',
};
---
<Base
  title="About Gio · The Operator Behind Vemor"
  description="Giovanni Vega Garcia spent 14 years managing smog stations, writing collision estimates, and adjusting claims before founding Vemor. This is why the automation works."
  schema={schema}
  path="/about"
>
  <section class="hero" style="min-height:0; padding-bottom:60px;">
    <span class="hero-tagline">About</span>
    <h1>Built by someone <span class="gold">who gets it.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      Vemor wasn't built by someone who read a blog post about small business.
      It was built by someone who spent 14 years inside one.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="story-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I'm Giovanni. Gio. First-generation college grad, son of immigrants who built
          their lives through work that nobody automated for them.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Six years managing smog station operations</strong>: three facilities, eighteen
          employees, test-and-repair, the counter, the phones, the vendors, the payroll.
          I know what it's like when the person answering the phone is also the person
          running the shop.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Eight years as a field claims adjuster</strong> for carriers you know: GEICO,
          Wawanesa, Farmers. Over a thousand shop visits across Southern California.
          Every day I watched owners juggle a customer at the counter, a tech with a
          question, and a phone ringing off the hook. I watched missed calls become
          missed revenue, one at a time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Then I taught myself to build. Python, automation, AI agents, databases,
          hardware. Not because I wanted to become a programmer, but because I kept
          seeing the same fixable problems and nobody was fixing them <strong>for the businesses
          I came from</strong>. The shops. The Spanish-speaking owners big tech ignores. The
          operators too busy working to shop for software.
        </p>
        <p>
          Vemor is the company I wished existed when I was the one closing out four
          registers at 9 PM.
        </p>
        <p class="gold" style="font-weight:600; font-size:1.1rem;">— Gio</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="story-stats">
          <div class="stat-card">
            <div class="stat-value">14+</div>
            <div class="stat-label">years in automotive operations and claims</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <div class="stat-value">1,000+</div>
            <div class="stat-label">shop visits as a field adjuster</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <div class="stat-value">MBA</div>
            <div class="stat-label">STEM-certified, University of San Diego</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <div class="stat-value">1st Gen</div>
            <div class="stat-label">college graduate</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:24px;">
          <ul class="feature-list">
            <li><strong>Bilingual, for real.</strong>&nbsp;English and Spanish are both native modes, for me and for everything I build.</li>
            <li><strong>Generative AI certificate,</strong>&nbsp;IE Business School: Unlocking Enterprise Value.</li>
            <li><strong>Studying what I practice.</strong>&nbsp;Preparing doctoral research on how small businesses make technology decisions they can survive. Every Vemor engagement feeds the work.</li>
            <li><strong>Builder.</strong>&nbsp;Self-taught, systems in production today: automation pipelines, RFID tracking, AI phone agents, legal document intelligence.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="section-full soft north-star">
    <p class="north-star-text">
      "Every credential on this page matters for one reason: <em>it makes the thing I build
      for you more likely to work.</em> That's the only test."
    </p>
  </div>

  <section style="text-align:center;">
    <h2 class="title">Let's talk.</h2>
    <div class="hero-ctas" style="justify-content:center;">
      <a href="https://Vemor.as.me/" class="btn-primary">Book a Call</a>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-secondary">Send a Message</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
